{
  "tema": 6235,
  "slug": "dudo-que",
  "titulo": "The subjunctive to express doubt or uncertainty",
  "subtitulo": "Dudo que venga. Es posible que llueva.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Expressions of doubt or uncertainty take the subjunctive, affirmative or negative: dudo que, es posible que, es probable que, es imposible que, puede ser que. Certainty (estoy seguro de que, es cierto que) takes the indicative.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When the main clause expresses **doubt, possibility or uncertainty**, the verb after **que** goes in the **subjunctive**, whether the main clause is affirmative or negative."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "dudo que",
              "texto": "_I doubt that_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "es posible / imposible que",
              "texto": "_it's possible / impossible that_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "es probable / improbable que",
              "texto": "_it's likely / unlikely that_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "es dudoso que",
              "texto": "_it's doubtful that_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "puede ser que",
              "texto": "_it may be that_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "temo que",
              "texto": "_I'm afraid that_"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When you're **certain**, use the **indicative**: **estoy seguro de que**, **es cierto que**, **es verdad que**, **no dudo que**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if you can't swear to it, put it in the subjunctive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Dudo que ==hayan tenido== mala intención.",
              "en": "I doubt they meant any harm."
            },
            {
              "es": "Es probable que ==comas== muchos mariscos en Ensenada.",
              "en": "You'll probably eat a lot of seafood in Ensenada."
            },
            {
              "es": "No es posible que ==se pierdan==.",
              "en": "There's no way they'll get lost."
            },
            {
              "es": "No es probable que ==haga== mal tiempo en Cancún.",
              "en": "It's unlikely the weather will be bad in Cancún."
            },
            {
              "es": "Es imposible que ==elija== ese camino para ir a la ciudad.",
              "en": "There's no way he'll take that road into the city."
            },
            {
              "es": "Temo que no ==llegues== a tiempo a tu entrevista.",
              "en": "I'm afraid you won't make it to your interview on time."
            },
            {
              "es": "Puede ser que los novios ==se casaran== en Haití.",
              "en": "Maybe the couple got married in Haiti."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "certeza",
      "titulo": "Certainty: indicative",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "indicativo",
                  "t": "Estoy segura de que llegaste a tiempo."
                },
                {
                  "v": "subjuntivo",
                  "t": "No estoy segura de que hayas llegado a tiempo."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Sure: indicative. Not sure: subjunctive."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "indicativo",
                  "t": "No dudo que tiene razón."
                },
                {
                  "v": "subjuntivo",
                  "t": "Dudo que tenga razón."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**No dudo** = I'm sure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Tal vez, quizás, a lo mejor** work differently: **a lo mejor** always takes the indicative (**a lo mejor viene**), and **tal vez / quizás** can take either."
        }
      ]
    },
